    "field": "Arctic sea ice science",
    "problem": "Previous projections of Arctic open-water periods are often limited to a single high-emission scenario and older climate models, failing to provide stakeholder-relevant, regional information for the lower warming thresholds targeted by international climate agreements.",
    "method": "This study analyzes CMIP6 model projections to quantify changes in regional Arctic open-water periods at multiple global warming thresholds, using the percentage of area with sea ice retreat/advance by specific dates to avoid biases in long-term analysis.",
    "task": "The task is to project future changes in the length and timing of regional Arctic open-water periods using CMIP6 climate models to assess the impacts at multiple global warming thresholds.",
